03} + 2^{2281} - 2 \\equiv -2 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}$.\n\nBy CRT, we need $n \\equiv 108 \\pmod{125}$ and $n \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}$.\n\n$n = 108 + 125k$. $108 \\mod 8 = 108 - 13 \\cdot 8 = 108 - 104 = 4$. So $4 + 125k \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}$. $125 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{8}$. So $4 + 5k \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}$, $5k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{8}$. $5^{-1} \\equiv 5 \\pmod{8}$ (since $5 \\cdot 5 = 25 \\equiv 1$). So $k \\equiv 10 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{8}$.\n\n$k = 2$: $n = 108 + 250 = 358$.\n\nLet me verify: $358 \\mod 125 = 358 - 2 \\cdot 125 = 358 - 250 = 108$ ✓. $358 \\mod 8 = 358 - 44 \\cdot 8 = 358 - 352 = 6$ ✓.\n\nSo the remainder is $\\boxed{358}$.\n\nLet me double-check the computation of $2^{81} \\mod 125$.\n\n$2^{100} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{125}$, order is 100.\n$2281 = 22 \\cdot 100 + 81$, so $2^{2281} \\equiv 2^{81} \\pmod{125}$.\n\n$2^{81} = 2^{81}$. Let me compute differently.\n$2^{10} \\equiv 24$\n$2^{20} \\equiv 76$\n$2^{40} \\equiv 76^2 = 5776 \\equiv 5776 - 46 \\cdot 125 = 5776 - 5750 = 26 \\pmod{125}$\n$2^{80} \\equiv 26^2 = 676 \\equiv 676 - 5 \\cdot 125 = 676 - 625 = 51 \\pmod{125}$\n$2^{81} \\equiv 51 \\cdot 2 = 102 \\pmod{125}$ ✓\n\nGreat, consistent.\n\nAnd $2^{2203} \\equiv 2^3 = 8 \\pmod{125}$ ✓ (since $2203 = 22 \\cdot 100 + 3$).\n\nSo the answer is $358$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787240438}
